<tool id="ampvis2_alpha_diversity" name="ampvis2 alpha diversity" version="2.4+galaxy1" profile="21.09">
  <description>calculate alpha-diversity indices for each sample</description>
  <macros />
  <xrefs>
    <xref type="bio.tools">ampvis2</xref>
  </xrefs>
  <requirements>
    <requirement type="package" version="2.4">iuc-ampvis2</requirement>
  </requirements>
  <version_command>Rscript -e 'cat(system.file("DESCRIPTION", package = "ampvis2"), sep = "\n")'</version_command>
  <command detect_errors="exit_code">
        Rscript '$__tool_directory__/alpha_diversity.R'
            '$input'
            '$output'
            $rarefy
            #if str($indices):
                --indices '$indices'
            #end if
            &gt; '$output'
    </command>
  <inputs>
    <param name="input" type="data" format="rds" label="Load an ampvis2 dataset" />
    <param argument="--rarefy" type="integer" value="1000" min="1" label="Rarefaction depth" />
    <param argument="--indices" type="select" multiple="true" display="checkboxes" label="Alpha-diversity indices">
      <option value="ace" selected="true">ACE</option>
      <option value="berger-parkerdominance" selected="true">Berger-Parker dominance</option>
      <option value="brillouinindex" selected="true">Brillouin index</option>
      <option value="chao1" selected="true">Chao1</option>
      <option value="chao1ci" selected="true">Chao1 confidence interval</option>
      <option value="doubleest" selected="true">Double estimator</option>
      <option value="doubleestci" selected="true">Double estimator confidence interval</option>
      <option value="enversheid" selected="true">Evensheid</option>
      <option value="fisheralpha" selected="true">Fisher's alpha</option>
      <option value="goodscoverage" selected="true">Good's coverage</option>
      <option value="heippeindex" selected="true">Heippe index</option>
      <option value="invsimpson" selected="true">Inverse Simpson index</option>
      <option value="jost" selected="true">Jost's D</option>
      <option value="mcintoshd" selected="true">McIntosh D</option>
      <option value="margaleffnumber" selected="true">Margaleff number</option>
      <option value="menhinick" selected="true">Menhinick</option>
      <option value="observedspecies" selected="true">Observed species</option>
      <option value="osd" selected="true">Order statistic dispersion</option>
      <option value="simpson" selected="true">Simpson index</option>
      <option value="simpsonreciprocal" selected="true">Reciprocal Simpson index</option>
      <option value="shannon" selected="true">Shannon entropy</option>
      <option value="simpson_e" selected="true">Simpson evenness</option>
      <option value="simpson_reciprocalsq" selected="true">Reciprocal square Simpson index</option>
      <option value="simpson_sqrt" selected="true">Square root Simpson index</option>
      <option value="singlespeciesfraction" selected="true">Single species fraction</option>
      <option value="stanley" selected="true">Stanley</option>
      <option value="tss" selected="true">Total sum of squares</option>
      <option value="unique" selected="true">Unique</option>
      <option value="vegind" selected="true">Vegindex</option>
    </param>
  </inputs>
  <outputs>
    <data name="output" format="tabular" />
  </outputs>
  <tests>
    <test>
      <param name="input" ftype="rds" value="picrust-test.rds" />
      <param name="rarefy" value="1000" />
      <param name="indices" value="ace,berger-parkerdominance,chao1,goodscoverage,jost,simpson,shannon,tss,unique" />
      <output name="output" file="alpha_diversity.tabular" ftype="tabular" />
    </test>
  </tests>
  <help>
What it does
============

Calculate alpha-diversity indices for each sample and combines with the metadata.

The Galaxy tool calls the `amp_alpha_diversity
&lt;https://kasperskytte.github.io/ampvis2/reference/amp_alphadiv.html&gt;`_ function
of the ampvis2 package.

Usage
=====

The alpha-diversity indices are calculated per sample using the vegan function `diversity &lt;https://rdrr.io/pkg/vegan/man/diversity.html&gt;`_,
where the read abundances are first rarefied using `rrarefy &lt;https://rdrr.io/pkg/vegan/man/rarefy.html&gt;`_ by the size of the rarefy argument.
Refer to the vegan documentation for details about the different indices and how they are
calculated.


Input
=====


        An ampvis2 RDS dataset obtained by the ``ampvis2: load`` tool (or ``ampvis2: mergereplicates`` or one of the
        ``ampvis2: subset ...`` tools).


Output
======

A tabular dataset containing the chosen alpha-diversity measures per sample.
    </help>
